  "kind": "CONTRACT",
  "status": "exists",
  "docs": {
    "purpose": "Lets an admin look up one property by address or internal ID and see everything the system has calculated about it — zoning limits, buildable size, renovation and addition cost estimates, and nearby comparable committee-of-adjustment decisions. This is the data behind the admin Parcel Cost Model Tool.",
    "data_story": "It reads 4 tables — `parcels`, `address_points`, `parcel_address_points` and `coa_applications` and writes nothing. Its response is an explicit pick-by-name projection of 157 fields, so a column added to a table upstream does not leak into the client by accident. It is called from 1 place: `src/features/admin-flight-center/api/useParcelLookup.ts`.",
    "under_126": "Becomes a **CONTRACT descriptor** of archetype `QUERY`. It declares its `database.reads[]` with named columns, its response projection as an explicit whitelist, its auth class, its rate bucket and its staleness — and `outputs.writes` is forced to `\"none\"`. Its `consumers[]` becomes the edge list of the fan-out graph — the join nothing in this estate holds today."
  },
